  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe central idea is to solve the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by employing a genetic algorithm that modifies a fixed-length binary sequence. This approach leverages the observation that optimal solutions often exhibit binary structures and can be constructed using combinatorial optimization techniques rather than continuous optimization. The genetic algorithm improves upon the parent solution by using crossover and mutation operations while maintaining a fixed length and Hamming weight. A repair function ensures the resulting sequences satisfy the integral constraint, and the evaluation function computes the maximum correlation between the sequence and its complement scaled appropriately.\n\nMathematical specification:\n- Representation: Binary vectors of length n (180) with exactly n/2 (90) ones and n/2 zeros.\n- Objective: Minimize C_5 = max_k (\u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx) \u2248 max_k [np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\")*(2/n)]\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 h_i \u2264 1 for all i and \u2211h_i = n/2 exactly.\n- Repair mechanism: After crossover or mutation, adjust the binary vector by flipping bits to exactly match the required sum.\n- Fitness evaluation: Uses the correlation score between h and its complement to guide selection.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n1. Validate parent solution if available: Convert to binary and enforce sum.\n2. Initialize population: Generate 50 binary vectors with required sum.\n3. Core loop:\n   a. Select parents via tournament selection.\n   b. Apply crossover (80% prob) or mutation (20% prob).\n   c. Repair children to enforce sum constraint.\n   d. Evaluate fitness using correlation.\n   e. Replace population or best individual based on fitness.\n4. After hyperparameter tuning, return best solution, its fitness, and n.\n\ndef iivolvevec(parent):\n    Convert parent to binary and repair to exact sum.\n\ndef repair_binary(vec, n, target_sum):\n    Maintain binary vector with exact sum target_sum after mutation/selection.\n\ndef calculate_fitness(vec):\n    Compute C_5 score using correlation with FFT for efficiency.\n\ndef run(seed=42, budget_s=1100):\n    Initialize run time and population.\n    While time permits and improvements:\n        Perform selection, crossover/mutation, and repair.\n        Update best solution if fitness improves.\n    Return best solution list, its fitness, and 180.\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Population size = 50\n- Crossover rate = 0.8 (balanced with mutation)\n- Tournament selection size = 3\n- Repair complexity = O(n) with bit flipping\n- Use FFT for efficient correlation (method='auto' in np.correlate)\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- Est. 5e6 operations/iterations (n=180)\n- Check time after each generation\n- Supply fallback solution if not improved\n- Use protection against numerical issues\n\nValidation and return contract:\n- h[i] in {0,1} exactly\n- Sum = 90 exactly\n- Fitness = C_5 score via correlation scaling\n- Reproduce exact evaluation of parent\n- Handle population stagnation",
